  "description": "Fun, fast and confidence-inspiring\nBuilt to unlock progression from the very first ride, Whyte Secta 26 MX junior hardtail brings proper trail performance to riders aged 12 years (137cm–152cm tall) and up. MX wheel sizing – 27.5in front for stability and confidence, 26in rear for agility and control – delivers a balanced, capable ride that helps young riders push further with confidence. A lightweight, tough frame and modern, progressive geometry make climbs more manageable and descents more controlled, while sharp, predictable handling keeps things fun on everything from local trails to bike park features. Simple, durable and purpose-built, it’s a bike designed to grow skills, confidence and ambition every ride.\n\nHighlights\n– Confidence-inspiring, progressive mountain bike geometry and handling.\n– Lightweight 6061 T6 precision formed aluminium, dropper post ready frame.\n– Suntour MAG32 100mm travel, 27.5in air-sprung suspension fork (with hydraulic lock-out + rebound adjustment).\n– Mixed 'MX' wheels (27.5in (front) + 26in (rear)) with WTB Trail Boss tyres (2.4in front, 2.25in rear).\n– Shimano Essa 1x8 (eight-speed) drivetrain (30T chainring x 11-45T cassette).\n– Tektro hydraulic disc brakes (160mm rotors front + rear).\n– Choice of two colours: purple or aqua.\n\nIdeal for… youth riders 12 years+ approx. (137cm–152cm tall) looking for a confidence-inspiring hardtail that’s ready for performance-enhancing upgrades as they progress.",
